lowing sets is a subset of $A={4n+1∣n\\in {0,1,2,3}}?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we must find the elements of the set $A.$ Substituting the values $n\\in {0,1,2,3}$ into the formula $4n+1,$ we get the following elements:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n=0 & \\,⇒\\,4(0)+1=1 \\\\ n=1 & \\,⇒\\,4(1)+1=5 \\\\ n=2 & \\,⇒\\,4(2)+1=9 \\\\ n=3 & \\,⇒\\,4(3)+1=13\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\nA={1,5,9,13}.\n$$\n\nNow, a subset of $A$ is a set whose elements are also elements of the set $A.$\n\nIn our case, $B={1,5,13}$ is a subset of $A.$\n\nIn the rest of the options, the set $B$ has elements that are not in $A,$ meaning that it is not a subset of $A.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-37264/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b0e5efaa-e624-5045-abdb-cdf8d32ad6cb"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-37264"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-1188/selection/cde4c0c1840c8aaf81d3dea2a76973ae354e76ffd6eda2e595160156e35f114c" :answer/id #uuid "7fe68fbe-52b1-5578-9d17-1d6d3e0ec5aa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{c,f}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-1188/selection/d29017b837160b02d6efde5de6bfc9abac4afb39dfa30ca9db1d9ee4b945515c" :answer/id #uuid "29cc7ea2-228f-5665-9b12-4fb701d32d12" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a,c,d,e,f}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-1188/selection/37b74e5e7c834ed9fe45a6771548f261fb468ab45cd2cbec4f5efe7ea7ac68f7" :answer/id #uuid "4a827ea2-e8b1-5186-91d7-2c27c85c4cf5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a,c,d}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-1188/selection/35e406b463d22fc69d241790aab2f1dc6ab059ac6d2cf5fce1772944aaf8ac07" :answer/id #uuid "cd6c6914-1b53-5c9a-aaa3-cc81b38cc552" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a,b,e}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-1188/selection/c2b21299279a17964c0b37775b3f97d88ee527611676cdb737b92ceca6c27f32" :answer/id #uuid "836a