s a subset of ${R}^{-}.$ Indeed, every negative rational number is also a negative real number.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-80829/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9b7f1d12-3335-5dd7-bf36-e07077d0c45d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-80829"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-1208/selection/215989083557a1941b3e400be3c26b782e7b1019c203e85bc44c02bf39db2daa" :answer/id #uuid "254d924b-bee0-53cc-b81e-11f74c39e6f7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "R⊆R" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-1208/selection/608aa8eee889cc9ba516a8468964f58babe8f298be2aea159122552581473af6" :answer/id #uuid "07e403f2-50ae-5018-9532-20b87d3ce2a4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "Q⊆R" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-1208/selection/83ecf189389cf3fc70f0747c1da38769a48a4b0abd4fc8cd441b40be21951c93" :answer/id #uuid "e97d5216-d55b-51c2-bf5a-fbe432e1a433" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "Z⊆R" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-1208/selection/7a6f4f327f737cd78c8959850e5227eb0c50880e6dc46d0cc035d8ea16983edb" :answer/id #uuid "111a0775-0e63-5119-9c08-061621c5a088" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{Z}^{+}⊆Z" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-1208/selection/c5779127aae119392a5a9971807e90a16aa987b0c7f51c2068092c398b224535" :answer/id #uuid "de302136-7644-5210-8f01-fd136225d27c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "C⊆Z" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-1208/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ad001e51-5715-5c03-a6d6-a251356622ec" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-1208/selection/c5779127aae119392a5a9971807e90a16aa987b0c7f51c2068092c398b224535" :answer-field/choices ["q-1208/selection/215989083557a1941b3e400be3c26b782e7b1019c203e85bc44c02bf39db2daa" "q-1208/selection/608aa8eee889cc9ba516a8468964f58babe8f298be2aea159122552581473af6" "q-1208/selection/83ecf189389cf3fc70f0747c1da38769a48a4b0abd4fc8cd441b40be21951c93" "q-1208/selection/7a6f4f327f737cd78c8959850e5227eb0c50880e6dc46d0cc035d8ea16983edb" "q-1208/selection/c5779127aae119392a5a9971807e90a16aa987b0c7f51c2068092c398b224535"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-1208" :question/id #uuid "23e8510c-99c3-539c-9c30-63245db2572b" :question/math-academy-id "q-1208" :question/problem "Which statement is **not** true?" :question/worked-solution "If $A⊆B,$ then $A$ is a subset of $B,$ meaning that every element of $A$ is an element of $B.$\n\nAmong the given choices, only $C⊆Z$ is not true. This statement is not true because not every complex is an integer number. For example, we have $2\\text{i}\\in C$ but $2\\text{i}\\notin Z.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-1208/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9b7f1d12-3335-5dd7-bf36-e07077d0c45d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-1208"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-105033/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "210d5fd3-52a4-5747-be08-1606c454ff88" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105033/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "011f8fa9-da1f-5562-95f3-5fb0340f573f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105033/selection/93198c2e65472148f49c73a47d70892e6efd0b46acbb489ee2afeea42a4a8c25" :answer/id #uuid "d09de186-f91d-5e49-bea5-eb0615dcbbd9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105033/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "78491162-0678-5759-b0c9-bc4216f09025" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105033/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "77ace381-105a-5a4c-8283-88d0f8afc465" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105033/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "7c004aee-b348-5189-ab95-0dc257eda440" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-105033/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer-field/choices ["q-105033/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-105033/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-105033/selection/93198c2e65472148f49c73a47d70892e6efd0b46acbb489ee2afeea42a4a8c25" "q-105033/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-105033/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-105033" :question/id #uuid "8ccd9d30-cbcf-53db-8687-8f45cfff87ad" :question/math-academy-id "q-105033" :question/problem "Which of the following are subsets of ${Q}_{0}^{-}$ (the set of non-positive rational numbers)?\n\n- $Z$\n- ${Z}^{-}$ (the set of negative integers)\n- $N$" :question/worked-solution "$A$ is a subset of $B$ if every element of $A$ is an element of $B.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect the given choices.\n\n- $Z$ is *not* a subset of ${Q}_{0}^{-}.$ For example, $1\\in Z$ but $1\\notin {Q}_{0}^{-}.$\n\n- ${Z}^{-}$ is  a subset of ${Q}_{0}^{-}.$ Every negative integer is a non-positive rational number.\n\n- $N$ is *not* a subset of ${Q}_{0}^{-}.$ For example, $1\\in N$ but $1\\notin {Q}_{0}^{-}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-105033/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9b7f1d12-3335-5dd7-bf36-e07077d0c45d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-105033"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-80837/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "44daf9f8-f887-560e-8dc2-1701ac875786" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80837/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "943eb759-043f-5bca-9812-c21371e4247e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80837/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "f1e4f21f-dbaf-5383-94a3-ce1f9a91f307" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80837/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "c3a2ec3b-6299-5b77-ab29-091cdaa78c35" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80837/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "32dcc32d-0549-5946-a845-8e14749b97b6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80837/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e18bdbef-2c6f-5188-813a-2fbd55072813" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-80837/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer-field/choices ["q-80837/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-80837/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-80837/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-80837/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-80837/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-80837" :question/id #uuid "0090583c-ee77-57f6-b6b6-20b90fcbdcc2" :question/math-academy-id "q-80837" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true for the sets $A={x\\in {Z}^{+}∣x\\le 3}$ and $B={x\\in Z∣0\\le x<3}?$\n\n- $A⊆B$\n- $B⊈A$\n- $∅⊈B$" :question/worked-solution "First, we must find the elements of the sets $A$ and $B.$\n\n- The elements of the set $A$ are all positive integers that satisfy the inequality $x\\le 3.$ So, we have \n\n$$\nA={1,2,3}.\n$$\n\n- On the other hand, the elements of the set $B$ are all integers that satisfy the inequality $0\\le x<3.$ So, we have\n\n$$\nB={0,1,2}.\n$$\n\nNow, let's inspect the given statements.\n\n- $A⊆B$ is false. For example, $3\\in A$ but $3\\notin B.$\n\n- $B⊈A$ is true. For example, $0\\in B$ but $0\\notin A.$\n\n- $∅⊈B$ is false. The null set $∅={}$ is a subset of *every* set.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-80837/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "495f3da0-849a-589d-ac88-26d6825445e4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-80837"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-1212/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "db3dca2c-cc00-5fac-9ef0-b9e22ae6f708" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-1212/selection/4c09ef323dd53803d71b0c6f839afd3fa7c67c7a3c52acd9fb673fd4aafc2a26" :answer/id #uuid "adfccc75-c1ca-5044-9513-ea6e9a4769eb" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, III, and IV only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-1212/selection/6578e6ba0baf24b357651e14e1811fc4e1af585d8babc3d67097617d0e105e7a" :answer/id #uuid "b5db533c-a1e2-51fa-9364-58492fcba2d2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III and IV only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-1212/selection/6f916d391661973b3a5a5637f8b1a58ee0365885b48c933d7fb44b8e52c8db65" :answer/id #uuid "ecd6fd09-b6ed-59ce-a4b8-ffcb5d35b050" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II, III, and IV only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-1212/selection/0aba8feb8e80d6993512d064e058711be97ecf2a5cf7dd862ab928425f31c38c" :answer/id #uuid "2346196b-3122-5e48-bad9-803abaca2c14" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and IV only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-1212/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "c5cd6c9e-f9af-52c6-b07a-250d38363d9a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-1212/selection/6f916d391661973b3a5a5637f8b1a58ee0365885b48c933d7fb44b8e52c8db65" :answer-field/choices ["q-1212/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-1212/selection/4c09ef323dd53803d71b0c6f839afd3fa7c67c7a3c52acd9fb673fd4aafc2a26" "q-1212/selection/6578e6ba0baf24b357651e14e1811fc4e1af585d8babc3d67097617d0e105e7a" "q-1212/selection/6f916d391661973b3a5a5637f8b1a58ee0365885b48c933d7fb44b8e52c8db65" "q-1212/selection/0aba8feb8e80d6993512d064e058711be97ecf2a5cf7dd862ab928425f31c38c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-1212" :question/id #uuid "e4922535-c18b-5ded-bfaa-a163a44445c9" :question/math-academy-id "q-1212" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true for the sets $A={x\\in N∣-1\\le x+1\\le 3}$ and $B={x\\in Z∣{x}^{2}\\le -2}?$\n\n- $A⊆B$\n- $A⊈B$\n- $B⊆A$\n- $A⊇B$" :question/worked-solution "First, we must find the elements of the sets $A$ and $B.$\n\n- The elements of the set $A$ are all the natural numbers that satisfy the inequality $-1\\le x+1\\le 3,$ that is to say, $-2\\le x\\le 2.$ So, we have\n\n$$\nA={1,2}.\n$$\n\n- On the other hand, the elements of the set $B$ are all integers that satisfy the inequality ${x}^{2}\\le -2.$ So, we have\n\n$$\nB=∅.\n$$\n\nNow, let's inspect the given statements.\n\n- $A⊆B$ is false, while $A⊈B$ is true. For example, $0\\in A$ but $0\\notin B.$\n\n- $B⊆A$ is true. The empty set is a subset of every set.\n\n- $A⊇B$ is equivalent to $B⊆A,$ which is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II, III, and IV only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-1212/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "495f3da0-849a-589d-ac88-26d6825445e4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-1212"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-80832/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "fc09e4cc-7d0a-5fed-8738-20dec76df9f1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80832/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "48e4bf35-5c06-5b1c-8696-11f535bda248" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80832/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "3e007842-49ad-5fca-b751-2ec8be7d84ff" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80832/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "b2a9ab72-020d-5396-8333-01a81f55d78f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80832/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "123f649c-dde0-556d-91ce-d94189a1a884" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80832/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "8d8700e1-65a3-5893-ba8a-9a9dea1279f5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-80832/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer-field/choices ["q-80832/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-80832/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-80832/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-80832/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-80832/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-80832" :question/id #uuid "27ec29c7-bd41-57b6-9534-8283a5c47ce0" :question/math-academy-id "q-80832" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true for the sets $A={x\\in N:1\\le x<6}$ and $B={x\\in N:3x<9}?$\n\n- $A⊆B$\n- $B⊆A$\n- $A⊈B$" :question/worked-solution "First, we must find the elements of the sets $A$ and $B.$\n\n- The elements of the set $A$ are all natural numbers greater than or equal to $1$ but less than $6.$ So,\n\n$$\nA={1,2,3,4,5}.\n$$\n\n- On the other hand, the elements of the set $B$ are natural numbers which satisfy the inequality $3x<9.$ So,\n\n$$\nB={1,2}.\n$$\n\nNow, let's inspect the given statements.\n\n- $A⊆B$ is false, while $A⊈B$ is true. For example, $5\\in A$ but $5\\notin B.$\n\n- $B⊆A$ is true. Every element in the set $B$ is an element of the set $A.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-80832/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "495f3da0-849a-589d-ac88-26d6825445e4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-80832"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-13196"] :question/worked-solution "To find every subset of $A,$ we list out every combination of elements within $A.$ \n\nWe can use the following diagram to visualize the process:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071627/assets/8323a4292a4f06d66d456bfce1906cbc7e9933a3fac41dd5fb643e13d25f6a6e.png)\n\nNote that we must include the empty set since it is a subset of every set.\n\nBy doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\emptyset, \\{a\\}, \\{b\\}, \\{c\\}, \\{a, b\\}, \\{a, c\\}, \\{b, c\\}, \\{a, b, c\\}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
